<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/inspector.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/inspector-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/inspector.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="799" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/policyholder-calculators/">Calculators</a></li><li aria-current="page">Claim File Readiness Grader</li></ol></nav><p class="tag">Free checklist · nothing stored</p><h1>Claim File Readiness Grader</h1><p class="lede">Appraisal rewards preparation. The claim file readiness grader scores your documentation, gives it a letter grade and lists what to fix before you demand appraisal.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Claim file readiness grader</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk with a South Dakota attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full itemized estimate, not just the summary page."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete, line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an itemized estimate from a contractor or independent estimator. A one-line bid won’t carry weight with a panel."><span>Do you have your own line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Gather every photo, note when each was taken and add current photos."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the storm or loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the paragraph titled ‘Appraisal’ in the conditions and note any time limits."><span>Have you read the appraisal clause in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ clause and put the date on your calendar."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Tarp, board up or dry out as needed and keep every receipt."><span>Have temporary repairs been made and receipts kept?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your current declarations page."><span>Do you have a current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure attics, wall cavities, basements and roof decking have been checked so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect letters, emails and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the numbers in the appraisal payoff estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Submit any requested proof of loss before its deadline."><span>If a sworn proof of loss was requested, has it been sent?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn line small" data-reset>Clear answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out grade-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="grade-card"><span class="grade" data-o="grade">–</span><span class="grade-pct"><span data-o="score">0</span>% ready</span><span class="hint">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></span></div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Still to do</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why readiness matters</h2>
<p>An appraisal award is binding on the amount of loss once two of three panel members sign. If key documents are missing when the panel meets, those gaps can lower the award, and you may not get a second chance. Grading your file first helps you avoid that.</p>
<h2>How the claim file readiness grader scores you</h2>
<p>Questions are weighted. Coverage acceptance, the carrier’s itemized estimate and your own itemized estimate count most, because a panel cannot work without them. Photos, policy knowledge and repair records come next. The grade is A for 90% and up, B for 75%, C for 60%, D for 45% and F below that.</p>
<h2>After you grade your file</h2>
<p>Work through the to-do list, then run the <a href="/policyholder-calculators/appraisal-payoff-estimator/">appraisal payoff estimator</a> to see whether the gap justifies appraisal. If both look good, an <a href="/appraiser-services/insurance-estimate-second-opinion/">insurance estimate review</a> is a sensible next step.</p>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is a low grade a bad sign?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Not on its own. It means your file needs work before appraisal, which is fixable.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do I need every item to start appraisal?</summary><div class="ans"><p>No, but the most heavily weighted items, such as both itemized estimates, matter a great deal.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my information stored?</summary><div class="ans"><p>No. Your answers stay in your browser.</p></div></details></div>
